Confirmed stable.

Fixed the atomicity bug in `dao/stream/ws.cljc:545` (`accept-slot!`): the queue grab, phase flip, and queue clear are now one `swap!` (capturing the pre-swap pending-frames via a volatile inside the update function), closing the gap where a frame could be erased or deposited out of order. Added `test/dao/stream/ws_test.cljc`'s `a-frame-before-acknowledgement-is-queued-and-replays-in-order`, which exercises exactly that scenario (a frame arrives while the server handle is still `:pending`, then the ack lands, then a second frame arrives — asserting the queued one is replayed first).

